.L15677:
    .string "defn"
.L15678:
    .string "special-form"
.L15679:
    .string "(defn name (param ...) body)"
.L15680:
    .string "Define a top-level function. Parameters may carry a type annotation: `(k Secret)`, `(n Int)`."
.L15681:
    .string "def"
.L15682:
    .string "special-form"
.L15683:
    .string "(def name value)"
.L15684:
    .string "Bind a name at top level: an immutable global, initialized in source order before `main`. Its type is not generalized (one type for every use)."
.L15685:
    .string "let"
.L15686:
    .string "special-form"
.L15687:
    .string "(let name value body)"
.L15688:
    .string "Bind `name` to `value` for the extent of `body`. Immutable; shadowing an outer binding is allowed."
.L15689:
    .string "tuple"
.L15690:
    .string "special-form"
.L15691:
    .string "(tuple elem ...)"
.L15692:
    .string "Build a tuple. The element types are part of its type, so `(tuple 1 2)` and `(tuple \"a\" \"b\")` are different types that cannot be mixed. Read elements with `tuple-get`."
.L15693:
    .string "tuple-get"
.L15694:
    .string "special-form"
.L15695:
    .string "(tuple-get t i)"
.L15696:
    .string "Element `i` of a tuple, counting from 0. An index past the end is E_INDEX_OUT_OF_BOUNDS; a receiver that is not a tuple is E_TYPE_MISMATCH."
.L15697:
    .string "let*"
.L15698:
    .string "special-form"
.L15699:
    .string "(let* ((name value) ...) body ...)"
.L15700:
    .string "Bind each name in turn, each in scope for the bindings after it and for `body`. Sugar for nested `let`, rewritten before module resolution."
.L15701:
    .string "len"
.L15702:
    .string "builtin"
.L15703:
    .string "(len x)"
.L15704:
    .string "Length of a String, List, Vec, Map or IntMap. Resolved while type checking to that type's own length function, so str-length, list-length, vec-len and map-size all still work. Anything else, including an Int or a tuple, is E_TYPE_MISMATCH naming the type."
.L15705:
    .string "vec"
.L15706:
    .string "special-form"
.L15707:
    .string "(vec elem ...)"
.L15708:
    .string "Build a Vec from its elements. One element type, taken from the first, so `(vec 1 \"two\")` is E_TYPE_MISMATCH. Sugar for a chain of vec-push."
.L15709:
    .string "map"
.L15710:
    .string "special-form"
.L15711:
    .string "(map key value ...)"
.L15712:
    .string "Build a Map from key/value pairs; an odd argument count is E_MALFORMED_FORM. Sugar for a chain of map-insert from map-new, so a repeated key keeps the later value."
.L15713:
    .string "int?"
.L15714:
    .string "builtin"
.L15715:
    .string "(int? x)"
.L15716:
    .string "True when the operand's static type is Int. Decided while type checking, because a value carries no type at runtime, and the operand is still evaluated. A receiver whose type is not known is E_CANNOT_INFER. The same for float?, bool? and string?; struct? is true for a defstruct and false for an ADT; alias? is false wherever inference has run, since aliases are transparent."
.L15717:
    .string "let-mut"
.L15718:
    .string "special-form"
.L15719:
    .string "(let-mut name value body)"
.L15720:
    .string "Bind a mutable name. `set!` may rebind it; this is the only route to mutation, since struct fields are immutable."
.L15721:
    .string "set!"
.L15722:
    .string "special-form"
.L15723:
    .string "(set! name value)"
.L15724:
    .string "Rebind a `let-mut` name. Direct field mutation -- `(set! (struct-get p \"x\") 5)` -- is rejected."
.L15725:
    .string "fn"
.L15726:
    .string "special-form"
.L15727:
    .string "(fn (param ...) body)"
.L15728:
    .string "Anonymous closure. Identical to `lambda`; captures are analyzed at compile time and recorded on the closure."
.L15729:
    .string "lambda"
.L15730:
    .string "special-form"
.L15731:
    .string "(lambda (param ...) body)"
.L15732:
    .string "Anonymous closure. Identical to `fn`."
.L15734:
    .string "if"
.L15735:
    .string "special-form"
.L15736:
    .string "(if cond then else)"
.L15737:
    .string "Two-armed conditional. Both arms are required and must agree in type."
.L15738:
    .string "cond"
.L15739:
    .string "special-form"
.L15740:
    .string "(cond (test body) ... )"
.L15741:
    .string "Multi-way conditional, tested top to bottom."
.L15742:
    .string "when"
.L15743:
    .string "special-form"
.L15744:
    .string "(when cond body)"
.L15745:
    .string "One-armed conditional; the absent arm yields unit. A core/core function, not a special form, so `body` is evaluated before the test. Written `(when cond)` before a match arm's body, it is a guard."
.L15746:
    .string "while"
.L15747:
    .string "special-form"
.L15748:
    .string "(while cond body)"
.L15749:
    .string "Loop while `cond` holds."
.L15750:
    .string "for"
.L15751:
    .string "special-form"
.L15752:
    .string "(for (i start) limit body)"
.L15753:
    .string "Counted loop. `(for (i 16) n body)` starts at 16 -- a bare `(for (i) ...)` starts at 0."
.L15754:
    .string "match"
.L15755:
    .string "special-form"
.L15756:
    .string "(match subject (Variant binding ... body) ...)"
.L15757:
    .string "Destructure an ADT. Non-exhaustive matches are a compile-time error; a `_` arm matches anything."
.L15758:
    .string "begin"
.L15759:
    .string "special-form"
.L15760:
    .string "(begin expr ...)"
.L15761:
    .string "Sequence expressions left to right; the value is the last one."
.L15762:
    .string "try"
.L15763:
    .string "special-form"
.L15764:
    .string "(try body (catch e handler))"
.L15765:
    .string "Catch a runtime panic and bind its message to `e`."
.L15766:
    .string "unwrap"
.L15767:
    .string "special-form"
.L15768:
    .string "(unwrap expr)"
.L15769:
    .string "Project the payload out of an `Ok`/`Some`, panicking on `Err`/`None`."
.L15770:
    .string "error"
.L15771:
    .string "function"
.L15772:
    .string "(error \"message\")"
.L15773:
    .string "Return `(Err message)`. Does not raise: handle it by matching. From core/result. To unwind to the nearest try/catch instead, use `panic`."
.L15774:
    .string "panic"
.L15775:
    .string "function"
.L15776:
    .string "(panic \"message\")"
.L15777:
    .string "Raise a runtime error with a literal message: unwind to the nearest `try`/`catch`, or print and exit(1) when there is none. From allocator."
.L15778:
    .string "assert"
.L15779:
    .string "special-form"
.L15780:
    .string "(assert expr)"
.L15781:
    .string "Panic unless `expr` is true. A condition is a Bool."
.L15782:
    .string "range"
.L15783:
    .string "special-form"
.L15784:
    .string "(range start end)"
.L15785:
    .string "Match pattern for an integer range, inclusive at both ends: `((range 1 9) body)` as a match arm."
.L15786:
    .string "with-resource"
.L15787:
    .string "special-form"
.L15788:
    .string "(with-resource (name acquire) body)"
.L15789:
    .string "Bind `name` to `acquire` for `body`, then call `(Drop.drop name)` on the way out, normally or before an error propagates (spec 12.9). An Int is a file descriptor, closed with file-close."
.L15790:
    .string "with-region"
.L15791:
    .string "special-form"
.L15792:
    .string "(with-region (arena :block N :align A :limit L) body)  (with-region (fixed :size N :align A) body)"
.L15793:
    .string "Allocate `body`'s values in an explicit region, released when `body` ends. A value that would outlive it is E_REGION_ESCAPE; a bad spec is E_REGION_SPEC; running out is E_REGION_EXHAUSTED."
.L15795:
    .string "deftype"
.L15796:
    .string "special-form"
.L15797:
    .string "(deftype Name (Variant Field ...) ...)"
.L15798:
    .string "Declare an algebraic data type. Generic parameters follow the name."
.L15799:
    .string "defstruct"
.L15800:
    .string "special-form"
.L15801:
    .string "(defstruct Name (field Type) ...)"
.L15802:
    .string "Declare a struct. Fields are immutable; build a changed copy rather than mutating."
.L15803:
    .string "defstruct+"
.L15804:
    .string "special-form"
.L15805:
    .string "(defstruct+ Name (field Type) ...)"
.L15806:
    .string "Declare a struct. Auto-derives all 6 prelude traits (Show, Debug, Eq, Ord, Hash, Clone) when no inline (:derive [...]) is present."
.L15807:
    .string "struct-get"
.L15808:
    .string "special-form"
.L15809:
    .string "(struct-get value \"field\")"
.L15810:
    .string "Read a struct field. It is a read only -- there is no field-assignment form."
.L15811:
    .string "make-struct"
.L15812:
    .string "special-form"
.L15813:
    .string "(make-struct Name field ...)"
.L15814:
    .string "Construct a struct from positional field values. Not typed by the checker yet (E_CANNOT_INFER): call the constructor instead."
.L15815:
    .string "make-variant"
.L15816:
    .string "special-form"
.L15817:
    .string "(make-variant (Type) Variant field ...)"
.L15818:
    .string "Construct an ADT variant explicitly; usually written as the bare constructor call."
.L15819:
    .string "trait"
.L15820:
    .string "special-form"
.L15821:
    .string "(trait Name (method (param ...) ReturnType) ...)"
.L15822:
    .string "Declare a trait: a set of method signatures a type can implement."
.L15823:
    .string "impl"
.L15824:
    .string "special-form"
.L15825:
    .string "(impl Trait Type (defn method (self ...) body) ...)"
.L15826:
    .string "Implement a trait for a type. A second impl of the same pair is E_DUPLICATE_IMPL."
.L15827:
    .string "impl-not"
.L15828:
    .string "special-form"
.L15829:
    .string "(impl-not Trait Target)"
.L15830:
    .string "Forbid implementing Trait for Target, or for any type implementing trait Target (E_IMPL_FORBIDDEN). No impl of Trait may return a value derived from a protected one, so wrappers cannot expose it either."
.L15831:
    .string "derive"
.L15832:
    .string "special-form"
.L15833:
    .string "(derive Type Trait ...)"
.L15834:
    .string "Derive Show, Debug, Eq, Ord, Hash or Clone. Every field's type must implement the trait (E_TRAIT_NOT_DERIVABLE)."
.L15835:
    .string "macro"
.L15836:
    .string "special-form"
.L15837:
    .string "(macro name (param ...) template)"
.L15838:
    .string "Define a macro. Expansion is innermost-first with gensym hygiene."
.L15839:
    .string "defmacro"
.L15840:
    .string "special-form"
.L15841:
    .string "(defmacro name (param ...) template)"
.L15842:
    .string "Define a macro; a spelling of `macro`."
.L15843:
    .string "list"
.L15844:
    .string "special-form"
.L15845:
    .string "(list expr ...)  [expr ...]"
.L15846:
    .string "A list literal: the Cons chain of the elements in order, evaluated left to right. Every element has one type; `[]` is Nil."
.L15847:
    .string "quote"
.L15848:
    .string "special-form"
.L15849:
    .string "(quote data)  'data"
.L15850:
    .string "Constant data: an Int, Float, String or Bool, or a list of them (nested lists allowed). A name inside is E_MALFORMED_FORM."
.L15851:
    .string "quasiquote"
.L15852:
    .string "special-form"
.L15853:
    .string "`data  ,expr  ,@list"
.L15854:
    .string "A list built from constant data, with `,e` inserting a value and `,@e` splicing a list. A bare name inside is E_MALFORMED_FORM. Macro templates are plain forms, not quasiquotes."
.L15856:
    .string "use"
.L15857:
    .string "special-form"
.L15858:
    .string "(use path/to/module)"
.L15859:
    .string "Import a module. Paths resolve against `stdlib/`, then the current file's directory."
.L15860:
    .string "module"
.L15861:
    .string "special-form"
.L15862:
    .string "(module name)"
.L15863:
